        ['Why compare examples?', 'It reveals different strategies and reduces copying', 'It guarantees one answer', 'It removes the audience', 'Two campaigns use different tones. What can be learned?', 'Visual choices depend on purpose and audience', 'One must be wrong', 'Colour has no effect'],
        ['What is the evidence sequence?', 'Describe, interpret, judge', 'Judge, copy, submit', 'Draw, erase, ignore', '“The red shape is placed centrally” is what?', 'Description', 'A final judgement', 'A production step'],
        ['How is analysis different from copying?', 'It extracts principles for an original response', 'It reproduces every feature', 'There is no difference', 'What is a responsible use of inspiration?', 'Explain the strategy and create new imagery', 'Trace the logo', 'Remove the source note'],
        ['What should an effectiveness judgement reference?', 'Purpose and intended audience', 'Only personal taste', 'The designer’s file name', 'A campaign is attractive but confusing. What should be judged?', 'Whether it communicates the intended message', 'Whether it uses enough colours', 'Whether it prints on A4']
